are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- You would get back the amount that you invested (0 % annual return).\\n- USD 10,000 is invested\\n- (*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at the recommended holding period your average return is projected to be 13.0% before costs and 11.6% after costs.\\n\\n|                | If you exit after the Recommended Holding Period   |\\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------|\\n| Total costs    | USD 130                                            |\\n| Cost impact(*) | 1.4%                                               |\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHigher risk\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit   |                                                             | If you exit after the Recommended Holding Period   |\\n|------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|\\n| Entry costs                        | 1.3 %of the amount you pay in when entering this investment | USD 130                                            |\\n| Exit costs                         | 0.5 %of your investment before it is paid out to you        | USD 50                                             |\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended Holding Period: 11 months 2 days, which corresponds to the product maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, Société Générale or an entity of its group ensures a daily secondary market during the life of the product by providing bid and offer prices expressed as percentages of the Nominal Value and the difference between the bid and offer prices (the spread) will not be more than 1.00% of the Nominal Value. If you want to sell the product before the Maturity Date, the price of the product will depend on market parameters at the time you wish to sell and you may sustain a partial or total capital loss. In unusual market condition, the resale of the product may be temporarily or permanently suspended.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the person advising on, or selling, the product can be submitted directly to that person. Any complaint regarding the product or the conduct of the product manufacturer can be submitted to Société Générale at the following address: SOCIETE GENERALE, Regulatory Information Department, 17 cours Valmy, 92987 PARIS LA DEFENSE CEDEX, FRANCE - SG-complaints-kid@sgcib.com (http://kid.sgmarkets.com).\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe latest Key Information Document is available online at http://kid.sgmarkets.com. This document may be updated as of the date it is first created and for as long as the product is available for purchase, including during the marketing period of the product, where applicable. Further risks and information about the product are detailed in the product prospectus in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2017/1129. The prospectus (including its summary in the relevant local languages annexed to the Final Terms when the context requires) is available online at http://prospectus.socgen.com, and/or may be obtained free of charge upon request by calling +33(0) 969 32 08 07.", "extractionResult": {"cap": null, "isin": "CH1513911870", "floor": null, "issuer": null, "currency": "USD", "issue_date": "2026-02-05T00:00:00Z", "trade_date": null, "coupon_rate": 9.3247, "distributor": null, "issue_price": 100, "strike_date": "2026-01-29T00:00:00Z", "product_type": "certificate", "upside_style": "Digital", "document_type": "KID", "maturity_date": "2027-02-05T00:00:00Z", "coupon_applies": true, "coupon_barrier": 100, "digital_amount": 9.3247, "downside_style": "Barrier", "minimum_payout": null, "coupon_interval": "Semi-Annual", "investment_type": "Yield Enhancement", "offering_closes": null, "product_subtype": "Worst-of Barrier Reverse Convertible", "settlement_type": "Cash", "autocall_applies": false, "autocall_barrier": null, "coupon_last_date": "2027-02-05T00:00:00Z", "knock_in_barrier": 75, "principal_amount": 1000, "put_strike_level": "75", "sales_concession": 1.3, "autocall_interval": null, "call_strike_level": null, "coupon_first_date": "2026-08-05T00:00:00Z", "global_identifier": null, "underlying_ticker": "NDX Index / SPX Index / SX5E Index", "autocall_last_date": null, "proceeds_to_issuer": null, "autocall_first_date": null, "issuer_call_applies": false, "product_description": "Worst-of Barrier Reverse Convertible Semi-Annual 9.3247% Conditional Coupon on NASDAQ-100 / S&P 500 COMPOSITE STOCK PRICE INDEX / EURO STOXX 50 | CH1513911870 | Barrier: 75% European | Autocall: None | Maturity: 2027-02-05 | USD | null", "digital_strike_level": 100, "final_valuation_date": "2027-01-29T00:00:00Z", "trading_jurisdiction": "France", "memory_coupon_applies": false, "initial_valuation_date": "2026-01-29T00:00:00Z", "additional_upside_style": null, "basket_weightings_unequal": false, "contingent_coupon_applies": true, "upside_participation_rate": null, "autocall_last_payment_date": null, "autocall_first_payment_date": null, "downside_participation_rate": 100, "knock_in_barrier_event_type": "At Expiry", "coupon_last_observation_date": "2027-01-29T00:00:00Z", "coupon_first_observation_date": "2026-01-29T00:00:00Z", "proportional_principal_amount": null, "aggregate_principal_amount_type": null, "autocall_settlement_date_offset": null, "autocall_step_up_down_frequency": null, "autocall_step_up_down_step_amount": null, "autocall_step_up_down_initial_amount": null, "knock_in_barrier_event_observation_type": "At Expiry Only"}, "extractionStatus": "done"}, {"id": "506b0d73-f4b4-4ea2-8730-2315eb6c0924", "name": "KID-AST-9g1YdNlylK_eng.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "d50a7ac7-bbf2-4cab-a6a9-c5377aab2782", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "dfa0ef96-189d-40b7-8fd5-0ba94a74775e/1776841910216_b69bfed7_KID-AST-9g1YdNlylK_eng.pdf", "tokenCount": 2085, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Key Information Document\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n## Barrier Reverse Convertible on Partners Group Holding AG\\n\\nISIN: CH1513911821\\n\\nMANUFACTURER: Société Générale, http://kid.sgmarkets.com, Call +33(0) 969 32 08 07 for more information\\n\\nCOMPETENT AUTHORITY OF THE MANUFACTURER: Autorité des Marchés Financiers (AMF) &amp; Autorité de Contrôle Prudentiel et de Résolution (ACPR) is responsible for supervising Société Générale in relation to this Key Information Document.\\n\\nDATE OF PRODUCTION OF THIS KID: 05/03/2026\\n\\nISSUER: SG Issuer  |  GUARANTOR: Société Générale\\n\\n## You are about  to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n| Product Currency   | CHF        |\\n|--------------------|------------|\\n| Listing            | None       |\\n| Minimum Investment | CHF 10,000 |\\n| Maturity Date      | 05/02/2027 |\\n| Capital Barrier    | 60%        |\\n| Coupon Type        | Fixed      |\\n| Final Barrier      | 100%       |\\n\\n## Underlying\\n\\n| Settlement Currency   | CHF                                             |\\n|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------------|\\n| Nominal Value         | CHF 10,000 per note                             |\\n| Issue Price           | 100% of the Nominal Value                       |\\n| Minimum Reimbursement | No, you can lose up to the full invested amount |\\n| Capital Barrier Type  | Observed continuously                           |\\n| Coupon                | 4.736% per annum                                |\\n\\n| Reference Underlying      | Identifier   | Relevant Exchange   | Currency   |   Initial Value |\\n|---------------------------|--------------|---------------------|------------|-----------------|\\n| Partners Group Holding AG | CH0024608827 | Six Swiss Exchange  | CHF        |           1,057 |\\n\\n## Type\\n\\nThis product is an unsecured debt instrument governed by English law.\\n\\n## Term\\n\\nThis product has a life span of 1 year.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\nThis product is a fixed term investment which is designed to provide a fixed coupon on a periodic basis. The capital redemption amount is linked to the performance of the Reference Underlying. Your capital will be fully at risk when investing in this product.\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\nOn each Coupon Payment Date, you will receive the Coupon.\\n\\n## Final Redemption\\n\\nOn the Maturity Date, you will receive a final redemption amount.\\n\\n- If a Capital Barrier Event has not occurred or the Final Level of the Reference Underlying is at or above the Final Barrier, you will receive:\\n\\n100% of the Nominal Value.\\n\\n- Otherwise, you will receive physical delivery of the Reference Underlying. The number of shares to be delivered will be equal to the Nominal Value divided by the Conversion Factor. If the number of shares to be delivered does not equal a whole number, the number of shares to be delivered will be rounded down and the remaining amount will be paid in cash. As the value of the physical delivery is expected to be below the value of your initial investment when you receive the delivery, you are therefore likely to suffer a partial or total loss of your invested amount in this scenario.\\n\\nThe Conversion Factor is equal to the Initial Value multiplied by 100%.\\n\\nA Capital Barrier Event occurs if the level of the Reference Underlying has been observed at or below the Capital Barrier at any time since the Initial Observation Date (including any time during a single business day).\\n\\n## Additional Information\\n\\n- The level of the Reference Underlying corresponds to its value expressed as a percentage of its Initial Value.\\n- The Final Level is the level of the Reference Underlying observed on the Final Observation Date.\\n- Coupons are expressed as a percentage of the Nominal Value.\\n- Extraordinary events may lead to changes to the product's terms or the early termination of the product and could result in losses on your investment.\\n- The product is available through a public offering during the applicable offering period in the following jurisdiction(s): Switzerland\\n\\n## Calendar\\n\\n| Issue Date               | 05/02/2026             |\\n|--------------------------|------------------------|\\n| Initial Observation Date | 29/01/2026             |\\n| Final Observation Date   | 29/01/2027             |\\n| Maturity Date            | 05/02/2027             |\\n| Coupon Payment Dates     | 05/08/2026, 05/02/2027 |\\n\\nThe Performance scenarios and costs of the product are presented over its Recommended holding period (which is less than one year). They are not comparable with Performance scenarios and costs of other product having a different Recommended holding period and being calculated on annualized basis.\\n\\n## Intended Retail Investor\\n\\nThe product is aimed at investors who:\\n\\n- Have specific knowledge or experience of investing in similar products and in financial markets, and have the ability to understand the product and its risks and rewards.\\n- Seek a product offering income and have an investment horizon in line with the recommended holding period stated below.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n- Are able to bear total loss of their investment and accept the risk that the Issuer and / or Guarantor could fail to pay the capital and any potential return.\\n- Are willing to accept a level of risk to achieve potential returns that is consistent with the summary risk indicator shown below.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## Summary Risk Indicator\\n\\nLower risk\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n4\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 11 months.\\n\\nThe actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 6 out of 7, which is the second-highest risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a high level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nInflation Risk : if the economic situation is characterized by a high inflation persisting throughout the life time of the product, then the 'real' return of the product, equal to its return minus the inflation rate, might be negative.\\n\\n## Performance Scenarios\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Market could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\nRecommended holding period:\\n\\nExample Investment:\\n\\n11 months\\n\\nCHF 10,000\\n\\nIf you exit after 11 months\\n\\n(Recommended holding period)\\n\\n| Scenarios    |                                                                                      |            |\\n|--------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\\n| Minimum*     | There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your investment |            |\\n| Stress       | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 3,574  |\\n|              | Percentage Return                                                                    | -64.3%     |\\n| Unfavourable | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 6,435  |\\n|              | Percentage Return                                                                    | -35.7%     |\\n| Moderate     | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 12,473 |\\n|              | Percentage Return                                                                    | 24.7%      |\\n| Favourable   | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 12,473 |\\n|              | Percentage Return                                                                    | 24.7%      |\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you may have to pay extra cost.\\n\\nThe % figures in the table represent the potential positive (green) or negative (red) returns you might achieve at the end of the recommended holding period (last column) or by selling the product before (previous column) and for a stressed, unfavourable, moderate and favourable scenario (per line). These scenarios were calculated using simulations based on the underlying's past performance.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF SOCIÉTÉ GÉNÉRALE IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nIf the Issuer defaults you may only claim any unpaid amount from Société Générale (the Guarantor). Should Société Générale default or file for bankruptcy, you may suffer a partial or total loss of the invested amount. If the Issuer and/or the Guarantor becomes subject to resolution measures in the form of the bail-in tool (\\"bail-in\\"), your claim may be reduced to zero, converted into equity or its maturity may be postponed. Please be aware that your Investment is not covered by any investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nPlease find the ratings of Société Générale at https://investors.societegenerale.com/en/financial-and-non-financial-information/ratings/credit-ratings.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## Costs over Time\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods. We have assumed:\\n\\n- You would get back the amount that you invested (0 % annual return).\\n- CHF 10,000 is invested\\n- (*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at the recommended holding period your average return is projected to be 24.8% before costs and 24.7% after costs.\\n\\n|                | If you exit after the Recommended Holding Period   |\\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------|\\n| Total costs    | CHF 5                                              |\\n| Cost impact(*) | 0.1%                                               |\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHigher risk\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit   |                                                             | If you exit after the Recommended Holding Period   |\\n|------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|\\n| Entry costs                        | 0.1 %of the amount you pay in when entering this investment | CHF 5                                              |\\n| Exit costs                         | 0.5 %of your investment before it is paid out to you        | CHF 50                                             |\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\n## Recommended Holding Period: 11 months, which corresponds to the product maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, Société Générale or an entity of its group ensures a daily secondary market during the life of the product by providing bid and offer prices expressed as percentages of the Nominal Value and the difference between the bid and offer prices (the spread) will not be more than 1.00% of the Nominal Value. If you want to sell the product before the Maturity Date, the price of the product will depend on market parameters at the time you wish to sell and you may sustain a partial or total capital loss. In unusual market condition, the resale of the product may be temporarily or permanently suspended.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the person advising on, or selling, the product can be submitted directly to that person. Any complaint regarding the product or the conduct of the product manufacturer can be submitted to Société Générale at the following address: SOCIETE GENERALE, Regulatory Information Department, 17 cours Valmy, 92987 PARIS LA DEFENSE CEDEX, FRANCE - SG-complaints-kid@sgcib.com (http://kid.sgmarkets.com).\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe latest Key Information Document is available online at http://kid.sgmarkets.com. This document may be updated as of the date it is first created and for as long as the product is available for purchase, including during the marketing period of the product, where applicable. Further risks and information about the product are detailed in the product prospectus in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2017/1129. The prospectus (including its summary in the relevant local languages annexed to the Final Terms when the context requires) is available online at http://prospectus.socgen.com, and/or may be obtained free of charge upon request by calling +33(0) 969 32 08 07.", "extractionResult": {"cap": null, "isin": "CH1513911821", "floor": null, "issuer": "SG Issuer S.A.", "currency": "CHF", "issue_date": "2026-02-05T00:00:00Z", "trade_date": null, "coupon_rate": 4.736, "distributor": null, "issue_price": 100, "strike_date": "2026-01-29T00:00:00Z", "product_type": "certificate", "upside_style": "Digital", "document_type": "KID", "maturity_date": "2027-02-05T00:00:00Z", "coupon_applies": true, "coupon_barrier": null, "digital_amount": 4.736, "downside_style": "Barrier", "minimum_payout": null, "coupon_interval": "Semi-Annual", "investment_type": "Yield Enhancement", "offering_closes": null, "product_subtype": "Barrier Reverse Convertible", "settlement_type": "Cash or physical", "autocall_applies": false, "autocall_barrier": null, "coupon_last_date": "2027-02-05T00:00:00Z", "knock_in_barrier": 60, "principal_amount": 10000, "put_strike_level": "60", "sales_concession": 0.1, "autocall_interval": null, "call_strike_level": null, "coupon_first_date": "2026-08-05T00:00:00Z", "global_identifier": null, "underlying_ticker": "PGHN SW", "autocall_last_date": null, "proceeds_to_issuer": 99.9, "autocall_first_date": null, "issuer_call_applies": false, "product_description": "Barrier Reverse Convertible Semi-Annual 4.736% Conditional Coupon on Partners Group Holding AG | CH1513911821 | Barrier: 60% European | Autocall: N/A | Maturity: 2027-02-05 | CHF | SG Issuer S.A.", "digital_strike_level": null, "final_valuation_date": "2027-01-29T00:00:00Z", "trading_jurisdiction": "Switzerland", "memory_coupon_applies": false, "initial_valuation_date": "2026-01-29T00:00:00Z", "additional_upside_style": null, "basket_weightings_unequal": null, "contingent_coupon_applies": true, "upside_participation_rate": null, "autocall_last_payment_date": null, "autocall_first_payment_date": null, "downside_participation_rate": 100, "knock_in_barrier_event_type": "At Expiry", "coupon_last_observation_date": "2027-01-29T00:00:00Z", "coupon_first_observation_date": "2026-01-29T00:00:00Z", "proportional_principal_amount": null, "aggregate_principal_amount_type": null, "autocall_settlement_date_offset": null, "autocall_step_up_down_frequency": null, "autocall_step_up_down_step_amount": null, "autocall_step_up_down_initial_amount": null, "knock_in_barrier_event_observation_type": "At Expiry Only"}, "extractionStatus": "done"}, {"id": "b4026057-c699-4ff7-bd27-496339757b43", "name": "KID-AST-9g1YO0AY1p_eng.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "56079245-ad5b-46c9-b36e-7bea6d32f562", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "dfa0ef96-189d-40b7-8fd5-0ba94a74775e/1776841910273_5379fc2b_KID-AST-9g1YO0AY1p_eng.pdf", "tokenCount": 2174, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Key Information Document\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n## Autocallable Worst-of Barrier Reverse Convertible\\n\\nISIN: CH1513910922\\n\\nMANUFACTURER: Société Générale, http://kid.sgmarkets.com, Call +33(0) 969 32 08 07 for more information\\n\\nCOMPETENT AUTHORITY OF THE MANUFACTURER: Autorité des Marchés Financiers (AMF) &amp; Autorité de Contrôle Prudentiel et de Résolution (ACPR) is responsible for supervising Société Générale in relation to this Key Information Document.\\n\\nDATE OF PRODUCTION OF THIS KID: 02/02/2026\\n\\nISSUER: SG Issuer  |  GUARANTOR: Société Générale\\n\\n## You are about  to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n| Product Currency         | CHF        |\\n|--------------------------|------------|\\n| Listing                  | None       |\\n| Minimum Investment       | CHF 1,000  |\\n| Maturity Date            | 03/02/2027 |\\n| Capital Barrier          | 65%        |\\n| Coupon Type              | Fixed      |\\n| Early Redemption Barrier | 100%       |\\n\\n## Underlying\\n\\nSettlement Currency\\n\\nNominal Value\\n\\nIssue Price\\n\\nMinimum Reimbursement\\n\\nCapital Barrier Type\\n\\nCoupon\\n\\nCHF\\n\\nCHF 1,000 per note\\n\\n100% of the Nominal Value\\n\\nNo, you can lose up to the full invested amount\\n\\nObserved on the Final Observation Date only\\n\\n7.5858%\\n\\n| Underlying               | Identifier   | Relevant Exchange                | Currency   |   Initial Value |\\n|--------------------------|--------------|----------------------------------|------------|-----------------|\\n| INFINEON TECHNOLOGIES AG | DE0006231004 | Frankfurt Stock Exchange (Xetra) | EUR        |         42.3939 |\\n| RHEINMETALL AG           | DE0007030009 | Frankfurt Stock Exchange (Xetra) | EUR        |      1,825.4756 |\\n| SIEMENS AG-REG           | DE0007236101 | Frankfurt Stock Exchange (Xetra) | EUR        |        253.7117 |\\n\\n## Type\\n\\nThis product is an unsecured debt instrument governed by English law.\\n\\n## Term\\n\\nThis product has a life span of 1 year but can be redeemed earlier according to the conditions indicated in the \\"objectives\\" section below.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\nThis product is designed to provide a fixed coupon on a periodic basis during the product life time. It is possible for the product to be automatically redeemed early based on pre-defined conditions. If the product is not redeemed early, the capital redemption amount is linked to the performance of the underlyings. Your capital will be fully at risk when investing in this product.\\n\\nThe Reference Underlying is the Underlying with the lowest observed level on the relevant observation.\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\nProvided that the product has not been previously redeemed early:\\n\\nOn each Coupon Payment Date, you will receive the Coupon.\\n\\n## Automatic Early Redemption\\n\\nOn any Early Redemption Observation Date, if the level of the Reference Underlying is at or above the Early Redemption Barrier, the product will be redeemed early and you will receive 100% of the Nominal Value, on the Early Redemption Payment Date.\\n\\n## Final Redemption\\n\\nOn the Maturity Date, provided that the product has not been redeemed early, you will receive a final redemption amount.\\n\\n- If the Final Level of the Reference Underlying is above the Capital Barrier, you will receive:\\n- 100% of the Nominal Value.\\n- Otherwise, you will receive the Final Level of the Reference Underlying multiplied by the Nominal Value. In this scenario, you will suffer a partial or total loss of your invested amount.\\n\\n## Additional Information\\n\\n- The level of each Underlying corresponds to its value expressed as a percentage of its Initial Value.\\n- The Final Level is the level of the Reference Underlying observed on the Final Observation Date.\\n- Coupons are expressed as a percentage of the Nominal Value.\\n- Extraordinary events may lead to changes to the product's terms or the early termination of the product and could result in losses on your investment.\\n- The product is available through a public offering during the applicable offering period in the following jurisdiction(s): Switzerland\\n\\n## Calendar\\n\\n| Issue Date                        | 03/02/2026             |\\n|-----------------------------------|------------------------|\\n| Initial Observation Date          | 27/01/2026             |\\n| Final Observation Date            | 27/01/2027             |\\n| Maturity Date                     | 03/02/2027             |\\n| Coupon Payment Dates              | 03/08/2026, 03/02/2027 |\\n| Early Redemption Observation Date | 27/07/2026             |\\n| Early Redemption Payment Date     | 03/08/2026             |\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Intended Retail Investor\\n\\nThe product is aimed at investors who:\\n\\n- Have specific knowledge or experience of investing in similar products and in financial markets, and have the ability to understand the product and its risks and rewards.\\n- Seek a product offering income and have an investment horizon in line with the recommended holding period stated below.\\n- Are able to bear total loss of their investment and accept the risk that the Issuer and / or Guarantor could fail to pay the capital and any potential return.\\n- Are willing to accept a level of risk to achieve potential returns that is consistent with the summary risk indicator shown below.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## Summary Risk Indicator\\n\\nLower risk\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 1 year.\\n\\nThe actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 5 out of 7, which is a medium-high risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium-high level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nInflation Risk : if the economic situation is characterized by a high inflation persisting throughout the life time of the product, then the 'real' return of the product, equal to its return minus the inflation rate, might be negative.\\n\\n## Performance Scenarios\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Market could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\nRecommended holding period:\\n\\n## Example Investment:\\n\\n## Until the product is called or matures\\n\\nThis may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table\\n\\nCHF 10,000\\n\\nIf you exit after 1 year\\n\\n| Scenarios                 |                                                                                      |            |\\n|---------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\\n| Minimum*                  | There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your investment |            |\\n| Stress                    | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 3,010  |\\n| Product ends after 1 year | Average return each year                                                             | -69.9%     |\\n| Unfavourable              | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 7,364  |\\n| Product ends after 1 year | Average return each year                                                             | -26.4%     |\\n| Moderate                  | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 11,602 |\\n| Product ends after 1 year | Average return each year                                                             | 16.0%      |\\n| Favourable                | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 11,602 |\\n| Product ends after 1 year | Average return each year                                                             | 16.0%      |\\n\\n(*) the return shown in the Minimum Scenario is the Minimum Reimbursement and does not include other type of return such as guaranteed coupon payments. The figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe % figures in the table represent the potential positive (green) or negative (red) returns you might achieve at the end of the recommended holding period (last column) or by selling the product before (previous column) and for a stressed, unfavourable, moderate and favourable scenario (per line). These scenarios were calculated using simulations based on the underlying's past performance.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF SOCIÉTÉ GÉNÉRALE IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nIf the Issuer defaults you may only claim any unpaid amount from Société Générale (the Guarantor). Should Société Générale default or file for bankruptcy, you may suffer a partial or total loss of the invested amount. If the Issuer and/or the Guarantor becomes subject to resolution measures in the form of the bail-in tool (\\"bail-in\\"), your claim may be reduced to zero, converted into equity or its maturity may be postponed. Please be aware that your Investment is not covered by any investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nPlease find the ratings of Société Générale at https://investors.societegenerale.com/en/financial-and-non-financial-information/ratings/credit-ratings.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHigher risk\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Costs over Time\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods.\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\n## We have assumed:\\n\\n- CHF 10,000 is invested\\n- a performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n|                       | If the product is called at the first possible date 03/08/2026   | If the product reaches maturity   |\\n|-----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\\n| Total costs           | CHF 36                                                           | CHF 36                            |\\n| Annual cost impact(*) | 0.4%                                                             | 0.4% each year                    |\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit   |                                                             | If you exit after the Recommended Holding Period   |\\n|------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|\\n| Entry costs                        | 0.4 %of the amount you pay in when entering this investment | CHF 36                                             |\\n| Exit costs                         | 0.5 %of your investment before it is paid out to you        | CHF 50                                             |\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\n## Recommended Holding Period: 1 year, which corresponds to the product maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, Société Générale or an entity of its group ensures a daily secondary market during the life of the product by providing bid and offer prices expressed as percentages of the Nominal Value and the difference between the bid and offer prices (the spread) will not be more than 1.00% of the Nominal Value. If you want to sell the product before the Maturity Date, the price of the product will depend on market parameters at the time you wish to sell and you may sustain a partial or total capital loss. In unusual market condition, the resale of the product may be temporarily or permanently suspended.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the person advising on, or selling, the product can be submitted directly to that person. Any complaint regarding the product or the conduct of the product manufacturer can be submitted to Société Générale at the following address: SOCIETE GENERALE, Regulatory Information Department, 17 cours Valmy, 92987 PARIS LA DEFENSE CEDEX, FRANCE - SG-complaints-kid@sgcib.com (http://kid.sgmarkets.com).\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe latest Key Information Document is available online at http://kid.sgmarkets.com. This document may be updated as of the date it is first created and for as long as the product is available for purchase, including during the marketing period of the product, where applicable. Further risks and information about the product are detailed in the product prospectus in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2017/1129. The prospectus (including its summary in the relevant local languages annexed to the Final Terms when the context requires) is available online at http://prospectus.socgen.com, and/or may be obtained free of charge upon request by calling +33(0) 969 32 08 07."}, {"id": "c1deb7c0-940e-46ca-8e0e-48b2b8765c12", "name": "KID-AST-9g1YODNjX6_eng.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "a1ba5a0a-54d6-4b44-91bb-912ebb1ac9c1", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "dfa0ef96-189d-40b7-8fd5-0ba94a74775e/1776841910113_b1732eab_KID-AST-9g1YODNjX6_eng.pdf", "tokenCount": 2399, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Key Information Document\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n## Autocallable Worst-of Reverse Convertible\\n\\nISIN: CH1513910393\\n\\nMANUFACTURER: Société Générale, http://kid.sgmarkets.com, Call +33(0) 969 32 08 07 for more information\\n\\nCOMPETENT AUTHORITY OF THE MANUFACTURER: Autorité des Marchés Financiers (AMF) &amp; Autorité de Contrôle Prudentiel et de Résolution (ACPR) is responsible for supervising Société Générale in relation to this Key Information Document.\\n\\nDATE OF PRODUCTION OF THIS KID: 02/03/2026\\n\\nISSUER: SG Issuer  |  GUARANTOR: Société Générale\\n\\n## You are about  to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n| Product Currency         | USD        |\\n|--------------------------|------------|\\n| Listing                  | None       |\\n| Minimum Investment       | USD 5,000  |\\n| Maturity Date            | 29/01/2027 |\\n| Capital Barrier          | 75%        |\\n| Coupon Type              | Fixed      |\\n| Early Redemption Barrier | 100%       |\\n\\n## Underlying\\n\\n| Settlement Currency   | USD                                             |\\n|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------------|\\n| Nominal Value         | USD 5,000 per note                              |\\n| Issue Price           | 100% of the Nominal Value                       |\\n| Minimum Reimbursement | No, you can lose up to the full invested amount |\\n| Capital Barrier Type  | Observed on the Final Observation Date only     |\\n| Coupon                | 0.7927%                                         |\\n\\n| Underlying        | Identifier   | Relevant Exchange     | Currency   |   Initial Value |\\n|-------------------|--------------|-----------------------|------------|-----------------|\\n| Apple Inc         | US0378331005 | Nasdaq Stock Exchange | USD        |          251.19 |\\n| AMAZON.COM INC    | US0231351067 | Nasdaq Stock Exchange | USD        |        239.0433 |\\n| ALPHABET INC-CL C | US02079K1079 | Nasdaq Stock Exchange | USD        |         329.215 |\\n\\n## Type\\n\\nThis product is an unsecured debt instrument governed by English law.\\n\\n## Term\\n\\nThis product has a life span of 1 year but can be redeemed earlier according to the conditions indicated in the \\"objectives\\" section below.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\nThis product is designed to provide a fixed coupon on a periodic basis during the product life time. It is possible for the product to be automatically redeemed early based on pre-defined conditions. If the product is not redeemed early, the capital redemption amount is linked to the performance of the underlyings. Your capital will be fully at risk when investing in this product.\\n\\nThe Reference Underlying is the Underlying with the lowest observed level on the relevant observation.\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\nProvided that the product has not been previously redeemed early:\\n\\nOn each Coupon Payment Date, you will receive the Coupon.\\n\\n## Automatic Early Redemption\\n\\nOn any Early Redemption Observation Date, if the level of the Reference Underlying is at or above the Early Redemption Barrier, the product will be redeemed early and you will receive 100% of the Nominal Value, on the Early Redemption Payment Date.\\n\\n## Final Redemption\\n\\nOn the Maturity Date, provided that the product has not been redeemed early, you will receive a final redemption amount.\\n\\n- If the Final Level of the Reference Underlying is at or above the Capital Barrier, you will receive:\\n- 100% of the Nominal Value.\\n- Otherwise, you will receive physical delivery of the Reference Underlying. The number of shares to be delivered will be equal to the Nominal Value divided by the Conversion Factor. If the number of shares to be delivered does not equal a whole number, the number of shares to be delivered will be rounded down and the remaining amount will be paid in cash. As the value of the physical delivery is expected to be below the value of your initial investment when you receive the delivery, you are therefore likely to suffer a partial or total loss of your invested amount in this scenario.\\n\\nThe Conversion Factor is equal to the Initial Value multiplied by the Capital Barrier.\\n\\n## Additional Information\\n\\n- The level of each Underlying corresponds to its value expressed as a percentage of its Initial Value.\\n- The Final Level is the level of the Reference Underlying observed on the Final Observation Date.\\n- Coupons are expressed as a percentage of the Nominal Value.\\n- Extraordinary events may lead to changes to the product's terms or the early termination of the product and could result in losses on your investment.\\n- The product is available through a public offering during the applicable offering period in the following jurisdiction(s): Switzerland\\n\\n## Calendar\\n\\n| Issue Date                         | 29/01/2026                                                                                                                                     |\\n|------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n| Initial Observation Date           | 26/01/2026                                                                                                                                     |\\n| Final Observation Date             | 22/01/2027                                                                                                                                     |\\n| Maturity Date                      | 29/01/2027                                                                                                                                     |\\n| Coupon Payment Dates               | 02/03/2026, 30/03/2026, 29/04/2026, 29/05/2026, 29/06/2026, 29/07/2026, 31/08/2026, 29/09/2026, 29/10/2026, 30/11/2026, 29/12/2026, 29/01/2027 |\\n| Early Redemption Observation Dates | 22/07/2026, 24/08/2026, 22/09/2026, 22/10/2026, 20/11/2026, 21/12/2026                                                                         |\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nEarly Redemption Payment Dates\\n\\n29/07/2026, 31/08/2026, 29/09/2026, 29/10/2026, 30/11/2026, 29/12/2026\\n\\nThe Performance scenarios and costs of the product are presented over its Recommended holding period (which is less than one year). They are not comparable with Performance scenarios and costs of other product having a different Recommended holding period and being calculated on annualized basis.\\n\\n## Intended Retail Investor\\n\\nThe product is aimed at investors who:\\n\\n- Have specific knowledge or experience of investing in similar products and in financial markets, and have the ability to understand the product and its risks and rewards.\\n- Seek a product offering income and have an investment horizon in line with the recommended holding period stated below.\\n- Are able to bear total loss of their investment and accept the risk that the Issuer and / or Guarantor could fail to pay the capital and any potential return.\\n- Are willing to accept a level of risk to achieve potential returns that is consistent with the summary risk indicator shown below.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## Summary Risk Indicator\\n\\nLower risk\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 10 months 27 days.\\n\\nThe actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 4 out of 7, which is a medium risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nBe aware of currency risk. You will receive payments in a different currency, so the final return you will get depend on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nInflation Risk : if the economic situation is characterized by a high inflation persisting throughout the life time of the product, then the 'real' return of the product, equal to its return minus the inflation rate, might be negative.\\n\\n## Performance Scenarios\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Market could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\nRecommended holding period:\\n\\n## Example Investment:\\n\\n## Until the product is called or matures\\n\\nThis may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table\\n\\nUSD 10,000\\n\\nIf you exit after 10 months 27 days\\n\\n| Scenarios                            |                                                                                      |            |\\n|--------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\\n| Minimum*                             | There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your investment |            |\\n| Stress                               | What you might get back after costs                                                  | USD 3,732  |\\n| Product ends after 10 months 27 days | Percentage Return                                                                    | -62.7%     |\\n| Unfavourable                         | What you might get back after costs                                                  | USD 8,896  |\\n| Product ends after 10 months 27 days | Percentage Return                                                                    | -11.0%     |\\n| Moderate                             | What you might get back after costs                                                  | USD 10,951 |\\n| Product ends after 10 months 27 days | Percentage Return                                                                    | 9.5%       |\\n| Favourable                           | What you might get back after costs                                                  | USD 11,425 |\\n| Product ends after 10 months 27 days | Percentage Return                                                                    | 14.3%      |\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe % figures in the table represent the potential positive (green) or negative (red) returns you might achieve at the end of the recommended holding period (last column) or by selling the product before (previous column) and for a stressed, unfavourable, moderate and favourable scenario (per line). These scenarios were calculated using simulations based on the underlying's past performance.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF SOCIÉTÉ GÉNÉRALE IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nIf the Issuer defaults you may only claim any unpaid amount from Société Générale (the Guarantor). Should Société Générale default or file for bankruptcy, you may suffer a partial or total loss of the invested amount. If the Issuer and/or the Guarantor becomes subject to resolution measures in the form of the bail-in tool (\\"bail-in\\"), your claim may be reduced to zero, converted into equity or its maturity may be postponed. Please be aware that your Investment is not covered by any investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nPlease find the ratings of Société Générale at https://investors.societegenerale.com/en/financial-and-non-financial-information/ratings/credit-ratings.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHigher risk\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Costs over Time\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods.\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\n## We have assumed:\\n\\n- USD 10,000 is invested\\n- a performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n- (*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at maturity your average return is projected to be 10.2% before costs and 9.5% after costs.\\n\\n|                | If the product is called at the first possible date 29/07/2026   | If the product reaches maturity   |\\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\\n| Total costs    | USD 57                                                           | USD 57                            |\\n| Cost impact(*) | 0.7%                                                             | 0.7% each year                    |\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit   |                                                             | If you exit after the Recommended Holding Period   |\\n|------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|\\n| Entry costs                        | 0.6 %of the amount you pay in when entering this investment | USD 57                                             |\\n| Exit costs                         | 0.5 %of your investment before it is paid out to you        | USD 50                                             |\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\n## Recommended Holding Period: 10 months 27 days, which corresponds to the product maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, Société Générale or an entity of its group ensures a daily secondary market during the life of the product by providing bid and offer prices expressed as percentages of the Nominal Value and the difference between the bid and offer prices (the spread) will not be more than 1.00% of the Nominal Value. If you want to sell the product before the Maturity Date, the price of the product will depend on market parameters at the time you wish to sell and you may sustain a partial or total capital loss. In unusual market condition, the resale of the product may be temporarily or permanently suspended.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the person advising on, or selling, the product can be submitted directly to that person. Any complaint regarding the product or the conduct of the product manufacturer can be submitted to Société Générale at the following address: SOCIETE GENERALE, Regulatory Information Department, 17 cours Valmy, 92987 PARIS LA DEFENSE CEDEX, FRANCE - SG-complaints-kid@sgcib.com (http://kid.sgmarkets.com).\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe latest Key Information Document is available online at http://kid.sgmarkets.com. This document may be updated as of the date it is first created and for as long as the product is available for purchase, including during the marketing period of the product, where applicable. Further risks and information about the product are detailed in the product prospectus in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2017/1129. The prospectus (including its summary in the relevant local languages annexed to the Final Terms when the context requires) is available online at http://prospectus.socgen.com, and/or may be obtained free of charge upon request by calling +33(0) 969 32 08 07."}, {"id": "bb78efd0-9a5d-45e5-99f1-4bfbb47571f4", "name": "KID-AST-9g1YOMdw4Z_eng.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "6b813650-5aa0-471c-89b4-cf417e56f9e2", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "dfa0ef96-189d-40b7-8fd5-0ba94a74775e/1776841911291_730120e7_KID-AST-9g1YOMdw4Z_eng.pdf", "tokenCount": 2149, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Key Information Document\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n## Worst-of Barrier Reverse Convertible\\n\\nISIN: CH1513910377\\n\\nMANUFACTURER: Société Générale, http://kid.sgmarkets.com, Call +33(0) 969 32 08 07 for more information\\n\\nCOMPETENT AUTHORITY OF THE MANUFACTURER: Autorité des Marchés Financiers (AMF) &amp; Autorité de Contrôle Prudentiel et de Résolution (ACPR) is responsible for supervising Société Générale in relation to this Key Information Document.\\n\\nDATE OF PRODUCTION OF THIS KID: 13/02/2026\\n\\nISSUER: SG Issuer  |  GUARANTOR: Société Générale\\n\\n## You are about  to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n| Product Currency   | CHF        |\\n|--------------------|------------|\\n| Listing            | None       |\\n| Minimum Investment | CHF 5,000  |\\n| Maturity Date      | 02/02/2027 |\\n| Capital Barrier    | 55%        |\\n| Coupon Type        | Fixed      |\\n| Final Barrier      | 100%       |\\n\\n## Underlying\\n\\n| Settlement Currency   | CHF                                             |\\n|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------------|\\n| Nominal Value         | CHF 5,000 per note                              |\\n| Issue Price           | 100% of the Nominal Value                       |\\n| Minimum Reimbursement | No, you can lose up to the full invested amount |\\n| Capital Barrier Type  | Observed continuously                           |\\n| Coupon                | 8.1956% per annum                               |\\n\\n| Underlying                | Identifier   | Relevant Exchange   | Currency   |   Initial Value |\\n|---------------------------|--------------|---------------------|------------|-----------------|\\n| Logitech International SA | CH0025751329 | Six Swiss Exchange  | CHF        |         72.8123 |\\n| Swiss Re AG               | CH0126881561 | Six Swiss Exchange  | CHF        |        122.2179 |\\n\\n## Type\\n\\nThis product is an unsecured debt instrument governed by English law.\\n\\n## Term\\n\\nThis product has a life span of 1 year.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\nThis product is a fixed term investment which is designed to provide a fixed coupon on a periodic basis. The capital redemption amount is linked to the performance of the underlyings. Your capital will be fully at risk when investing in this product.\\n\\nThe Reference Underlying is the Underlying with the lowest observed level on the relevant observation.\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\nOn each Coupon Payment Date, you will receive the Coupon.\\n\\n## Final Redemption\\n\\nOn the Maturity Date, you will receive a final redemption amount.\\n\\n- If a Capital Barrier Event has not occurred or the Final Level of the Reference Underlying is at or above the Final Barrier, you will receive:\\n\\n100% of the Nominal Value.\\n\\n- Otherwise, you will receive physical delivery of the Reference Underlying. The number of shares to be delivered will be equal to the Nominal Value divided by the Conversion Factor. If the number of shares to be delivered does not equal a whole number, the number of shares to be delivered will be rounded down and the remaining amount will be paid in cash. As the value of the physical delivery is expected to be below the value of your initial investment when you receive the delivery, you are therefore likely to suffer a partial or total loss of your invested amount in this scenario.\\n\\nThe Conversion Factor is equal to the Initial Value multiplied by 100%.\\n\\nA Capital Barrier Event occurs if the level of any of the underlyings have been observed at or below the Capital Barrier at any time since the Initial Observation Date (including any time during a single business day).\\n\\n## Additional Information\\n\\n- The level of each Underlying corresponds to its value expressed as a percentage of its Initial Value.\\n- The Final Level is the level of the Reference Underlying observed on the Final Observation Date.\\n- Coupons are expressed as a percentage of the Nominal Value.\\n- Extraordinary events may lead to changes to the product's terms or the early termination of the product and could result in losses on your investment.\\n- The product is available through a public offering during the applicable offering period in the following jurisdiction(s): Switzerland\\n\\n## Calendar\\n\\n| Issue Date               | 02/02/2026             |\\n|--------------------------|------------------------|\\n| Initial Observation Date | 26/01/2026             |\\n| Final Observation Date   | 26/01/2027             |\\n| Maturity Date            | 02/02/2027             |\\n| Coupon Payment Dates     | 03/08/2026, 02/02/2027 |\\n\\nThe Performance scenarios and costs of the product are presented over its Recommended holding period (which is less than one year). They are not comparable with Performance scenarios and costs of other product having a different Recommended holding period and being calculated on annualized basis.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Intended Retail Investor\\n\\nThe product is aimed at investors who:\\n\\n- Have specific knowledge or experience of investing in similar products and in financial markets, and have the ability to understand the product and its risks and rewards.\\n- Seek a product offering income and have an investment horizon in line with the recommended holding period stated below.\\n- Are able to bear total loss of their investment and accept the risk that the Issuer and / or Guarantor could fail to pay the capital and any potential return.\\n- Are willing to accept a level of risk to achieve potential returns that is consistent with the summary risk indicator shown below.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## Summary Risk Indicator\\n\\nLower risk\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 11 months 20 days.\\n\\nThe actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 6 out of 7, which is the second-highest risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a high level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nInflation Risk : if the economic situation is characterized by a high inflation persisting throughout the life time of the product, then the 'real' return of the product, equal to its return minus the inflation rate, might be negative.\\n\\n## Performance Scenarios\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Market could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\nRecommended holding period:\\n\\nExample Investment:\\n\\n11 months 20 days\\n\\nCHF 10,000\\n\\nIf you exit after 11 months 20 days\\n\\n(Recommended holding period)\\n\\n| Scenarios    |                                                                                      |            |\\n|--------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\\n| Minimum*     | There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your investment |            |\\n| Stress       | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 3,017  |\\n|              | Percentage Return                                                                    | -69.8%     |\\n| Unfavourable | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 5,946  |\\n|              | Percentage Return                                                                    | -40.5%     |\\n| Moderate     | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 10,798 |\\n|              | Percentage Return                                                                    | 8.0%       |\\n| Favourable   | What you might get back after costs                                                  | CHF 10,798 |\\n|              | Percentage Return                                                                    | 8.0%       |\\n\\n(*) the return shown in the Minimum Scenario is the Minimum Reimbursement and does not include other type of return such as guaranteed coupon payments. The figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you may have to pay extra cost.\\n\\nThe % figures in the table represent the potential positive (green) or negative (red) returns you might achieve at the end of the recommended holding period (last column) or by selling the product before (previous column) and for a stressed, unfavourable, moderate and favourable scenario (per line). These scenarios were calculated using simulations based on the underlying's past performance.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF SOCIÉTÉ GÉNÉRALE IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nIf the Issuer defaults you may only claim any unpaid amount from Société Générale (the Guarantor). Should Société Générale default or file for bankruptcy, you may suffer a partial or total loss of the invested amount. If the Issuer and/or the Guarantor becomes subject to resolution measures in the form of the bail-in tool (\\"bail-in\\"), your claim may be reduced to zero, converted into equity or its maturity may be postponed. Please be aware that your Investment is not covered by any investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nPlease find the ratings of Société Générale at https://investors.societegenerale.com/en/financial-and-non-financial-information/ratings/credit-ratings.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHigher risk\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Costs over Time\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods. We have assumed:\\n\\n- You would get back the amount that you invested (0 % annual return).\\n- CHF 10,000 is invested\\n\\n|                | If you exit after the Recommended Holding Period   |\\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------|\\n| Total costs    | CHF 16                                             |\\n| Cost impact(*) | 0.2%                                               |\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit   |                                                             | If you exit after the Recommended Holding Period   |\\n|------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|\\n| Entry costs                        | 0.2 %of the amount you pay in when entering this investment | CHF 16                                             |\\n| Exit costs                         | 0.5 %of your investment before it is paid out to you        | CHF 50                                             |\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\n## Recommended Holding Period: 11 months 20 days, which corresponds to the product maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, Société Générale or an entity of its group ensures a daily secondary market during the life of the product by providing bid and offer prices expressed as percentages of the Nominal Value and the difference between the bid and offer prices (the spread) will not be more than 1.00% of the Nominal Value. If you want to sell the product before the Maturity Date, the price of the product will depend on market parameters at the time you wish to sell and you may sustain a partial or total capital loss. In unusual market condition, the resale of the product may be temporarily or permanently suspended.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the person advising on, or selling, the product can be submitted directly to that person. Any complaint regarding the product or the conduct of the product manufacturer can be submitted to Société Générale at the following address: SOCIETE GENERALE, Regulatory Information Department, 17 cours Valmy, 92987 PARIS LA DEFENSE CEDEX, FRANCE - SG-complaints-kid@sgcib.com (http://kid.sgmarkets.com).\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe latest Key Information Document is available online at http://kid.sgmarkets.com. This document may be updated as of the date it is first created and for as long as the product is available for purchase, including during the marketing period of the product, where applicable. Further risks and information about the product are detailed in the product prospectus in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2017/1129. The prospectus (including its summary in the relevant local languages annexed to the Final Terms when the context requires) is available online at http://prospectus.socgen.com, and/or may be obtained free of charge upon request by calling +33(0) 969 32 08 07."}, {"id": "6a67c3e0-362f-4b54-937a-bb6b592434f6", "name": "KID-AST-9g1YY4Vg8Z_eng.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "f6821875-0382-447c-a2e5-1283bd778955", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "dfa0ef96-189d-40b7-8fd5-0ba94a74775e/1776841910374_f385e62f_KID-AST-9g1YY4Vg8Z_eng.pdf", "tokenCount": 2099, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Key Information Document\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n## Barrier Reverse Convertible on RWE AG\\n\\nISIN: CH1513910450\\n\\nMANUFACTURER: Société Générale, http://kid.sgmarkets.com, Call +33(0) 969 32 08 07 for more information\\n\\nCOMPETENT AUTHORITY OF THE MANUFACTURER: Autorité des Marchés Financiers (AMF) &amp; Autorité de Contrôle Prudentiel et de Résolution (ACPR) is responsible for supervising Société Générale in relation to this Key Information Document.\\n\\nDATE OF PRODUCTION OF THIS KID: 24/02/2026\\n\\nISSUER: SG Issuer  |  GUARANTOR: Société Générale\\n\\n## You are about  to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n| Product Currency   | EUR        |\\n|--------------------|------------|\\n| Listing            | None       |\\n| Minimum Investment | EUR 1,000  |\\n| Maturity Date      | 09/09/2026